<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Box code -> eSKD element name.

    The eSKD XML used to be built from ``row.kpi.name`` (the MIS Builder KPI
    name was literally the Skatteverket element name. That coupling is exactly
    what this change removes: the report now identifies a box by its ``code``
    (se_05, se_10, ...), and this table maps that code to the element name the
    DTD expects.

    Keeping it as data means:
      * the XML export has no knowledge of MIS or of Swedish box numbering,
      * a Skatteverket DTD revision is a data change, not a code change,
      * the 29 boxes are auditable in one place.

    Element names verified against the eSKD Upload DTD 6.0 and against the
    element names the previous implementation emitted (they were the MIS KPI
    names, which had been chosen to match the DTD).
-->
